## SQ-CBC-01 | chain: CD transition items, no incomplete-item errors
@group A (chain)
@commands boot; `shell grep -h "transition items" logs/kubejs/startup.log`; `shell grep -c "not registered - add a row\|no incomplete item registered" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass `[creativedelight] transition items (80)`; 0 incomplete errors (r1106cbb cooking boot: 63 + 9)
@fails `cd_transition_items.js` not loaded (jar startup scripts) or a CD assembly keyed on a row still in Engineering's `transition_items.js`
@from batches/r1106cbp/p1_chain.qb
shell grep -h "transition items" logs/kubejs/startup.log
shell grep -qE '\[creativedelight\] transition items \(89\)' logs/kubejs/startup.log  # startup.log (r1106spf: kjsexpect reads server.log)
shell grep -c "not registered - add a row\|no incomplete item registered" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log; true
shell test "$(cat logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -c "not registered - add a row\|no incomplete item registered")" = 0

## SQ-CBC-02 | cooking: NCH failures and absent-mods summary
@group A (cooking)
@commands boot; `shell grep -h "failed and was skipped" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log \| sed -E 's/[0-9]+//g' \| sort \| uniq -c \| sort -rn`; `shell grep -h "absent mods" logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass no `Empty array?` lines (r1106cbb: 81), no `grown_*`, `twig_nest`, `rope_to__air`, `canned_mulberry_pie_filling_pie` lines; total under 40 (was 230); record what is left; `[absent mods]` lines name absent mods (expected among them `quark`, `upgrade_aquatic`, `bushierflowers`)
@fails an `Empty array?` left: a filter key other than `input` / `output`, or a list filter (left to KubeJS on purpose); no `[absent mods]` line at all: `absent_mods.js` listener not running (it now always prints one line)
@from batches/r1106cbp/p2_cooking.qb
shell grep -h "failed and was skipped" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | sed -E 's/[0-9]+//g' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -40
shell grep -h "failed and was skipped" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | wc -l
shell ! grep -h "failed and was skipped" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -E "Empty array\?|grown_|twig_nest|rope_to__air|canned_mulberry_pie_filling_pie"
shell test "$(cat logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -c "failed and was skipped")" -lt 40
shell grep -h "absent mods" logs/kubejs/server.log
kjsexpect absent mods
look record what is left; [absent mods] names quark, upgrade_aquatic, bushierflowers among others

## SQ-CBC-03 | chain: failed-recipe count under 50
@group A (chain)
@commands `shell grep -h "Added [0-9]* recipes" logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass failed-recipe count under 50 (r1106cbb: 204, the `create:deploying` steps built from the missing incomplete items)
@fails `logErroringRecipes=true` in `srv/local/kubejs/dev.properties` and group the rest by script (open issue 2.2 #2)
@from batches/r1106cbp/p1_chain.qb passed
shell grep -h "Added [0-9]* recipes" logs/kubejs/server.log
shell n=$(grep -oE "[0-9]+ failed" logs/kubejs/server.log | tail -1 | grep -oE "[0-9]+"); echo "failed=${n:-0}"; test "${n:-0}" -lt 50

## SQ-CBC-04 | full pack: transition items split, removed count, sequenced assembly count
@group B (full pack)
@commands boot; `shell grep -h "transition items" logs/kubejs/startup.log`; `shell grep -h "Added [0-9]* recipes" logs/kubejs/server.log`; `shell grep -h "absent mods" logs/kubejs/server.log`; `> zq recipes creativeengineering:createsequencedassembly/` count, compare with `kubejs/exported/recipes`
@pass CD line 80 and Engineering's own count line (80 fewer than before); removed 1328 as r1106cbb boot 4; sequenced assembly count unchanged; `[absent mods]` prints `none skipped` or only mods truly absent from the pack
@fails a row lost in the move (compare both row lists with git)
@from batches/r1106cbo/c4_full.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
shell grep -h "transition items" logs/kubejs/startup.log
shell grep -qE '\[creativedelight\] transition items \(89\)' logs/kubejs/startup.log  # startup.log (r1106spf: kjsexpect reads server.log)
shell grep -h "Added [0-9]* recipes" logs/kubejs/server.log
shell n=$(grep -oE "removed [0-9]+ recipes" logs/kubejs/server.log | tail -1 | grep -oE "[0-9]+"); echo "removed=$n"; test "$n" -gt 1100 -a "$n" -lt 1600
shell grep -h "absent mods" logs/kubejs/server.log
shell grep -c "not registered - add a row\|no incomplete item registered" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log; true
> cdevtest bytype create:sequenced_assembly max=1
expect verb=bytype serializer=create:sequenced_assembly n=296$
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ done=0
look sequenced assembly count against 296 (2026-11-05 dump); [absent mods] never prints (afterRecipes not posted, run notes 14:06)

## SQ-CBC-05
@group A (chain)
@commands new OUT: `NOUPSTREAM=vinery_upstream port_chain.sh server OUT cbc05 A chain`; boot; wait for `Stopping\|crash`
@pass `bootexpect Vinery \(Creative Brewing\)` in the missing-jar message; no `Backport`
@fails `UpstreamJars.verifyOrFail` label
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# setup: NOUPSTREAM=vinery_upstream port_chain.sh server OUT cbc05 A chain; boot and wait for Stopping or a crash, not Done (as SQ-CBA-13)
bootexpect missing: .*vinery_upstream
bootexpect Vinery \(Creative Brewing\)
bootreject Backport
bootreject Done \(
shell grep -nE "missing: |get it from|Vinery \(Creative Brewing\)" logs/latest.log | head -5 | cut -c1-300
## SQ-CBC-06
@phase worldgen
@group B (instance + Creative Worldgen)
@commands new OUT with Creative Worldgen and its world generation mods but `DROP="GeophilicReforged-*.jar"`; boot
@pass `bootexpect Missing or unsupported mandatory dependencies`; `geophilic_reforged` listed for `creativeworldgen`
@fails Worldgen `mods.toml` entry
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# setup: DROP="GeophilicReforged-*.jar" ADD="creativeworldgen-*.jar" port_chain.sh server OUT cbc06 B instance (Creative Worldgen and its world generation mods from the pack, Geophilic left out); boot and wait for Stopping or a crash
bootexpect Missing or unsupported mandatory dependencies
bootexpect geophilic_reforged
bootreject Done \(
shell grep -nE "Missing or unsupported|Mod ID: 'geophilic_reforged'|Requested by: 'creativeworldgen'" logs/latest.log | head -8 | cut -c1-300
look geophilic_reforged is listed for creativeworldgen (Requested by line); if other Worldgen dependencies are listed too, ADD their jars and rerun
## SQ-CBC-07 | chain: no dependency or ordering error for creativebrewing
@group A (chain)
@commands the SQ-CBC-01 boot: `shell grep -c "creativebrewing" logs/latest.log` near `Missing or unsupported`; in the full-pack boot (SQ-CBC-04) the same
@pass no dependency error for creativebrewing in either (the 24 optional entries never stop a boot); no `cycle` / `ordering` error from FML
@fails an optional entry with a wrong mod id is harmless; an ordering cycle names the mod: drop its `ordering`
@from batches/r1106cbp/p1_chain.qb passed
bootreject Missing or unsupported mandatory
bootreject \b[Cc]ycle\b|[Oo]rdering (cycle|error|constraint)
shell grep -n "creativebrewing" logs/latest.log | grep -iE "depend|missing|unsupported|cycle" | head

## CQ-CBC-01
@group client (full pack)
@commands JEI: search `incomplete`; open the sequenced assembly page of a cod roll, a large meal (omurice) and an enchanted golden apple
@pass LOOK: the incomplete items keep their names and tinted sprites; the three assemblies list as before
@fails a moved row's texture override lost
@reviewed 2026-11-16
do {"wait": "jei"}
do {"screen": "jei_recipes:minecraft:enchanted_golden_apple"}
shot egapple_assembly
do {"screen": "jei_uses:create:sequenced_assembly"}
do {"screen": "close"}
do {"tooltip_text": "creativedelight:incomplete_omurice", "reject": "item\\.creative"}
look incomplete items keep their names and tinted sprites; cod roll, omurice and the enchanted golden apple assemblies list as before (open the other two pages by hand if the ids differ)
